# OpenHaC: stretch before manifests

When planning or implementing **incremental** work (e.g. “next N tickets” batches):

1. **Prefer stretch / future items** called out in [docs/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md](docs/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md) per-ID **Notes**, [docs/PRODUCTION_READINESS_SPEC.md](docs/PRODUCTION_READINESS_SPEC.md) **Future** sections, and [docs/ARCHITECTURE.md](docs/ARCHITECTURE.md) “still future” notes — **before** adding new **manifest-only** traceability (`str002_*`, `lib003_*`, etc.) keys.

2. **Manifest additions** are appropriate when they **support** a stretch (e.g. new pipeline artifact needs audit fields), fix a bug, or satisfy an explicit user request — not as the default batch filler.

3. If no stretch is in scope for a slice, say so briefly and propose a **concrete** stretch to tackle next instead of defaulting to manifest strings.
